      "content": "That’s getting much closer to the vibe I need. It’s a lot more chilling when he uses that pseudo-scientific justification.\n\nTo really drive home the \"natural order\" aspect, can you add a part where he explains why it's actually dangerous for society if they ever *did* try to rise up? Like, if you give too much responsibility to a group that's built for instinct rather than intellect, it doesn't just lead to failure, but to total social chaos or even \"degradation\" of the civilization. I want him to argue that their very nature is a threat to the stability the \"superior\" class has built.",
